        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: జ్వరం",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "జ్వరం (jvaraṁ) — \"a fever\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "నాకు జ్వరం (jvaraṁ) వచ్చింది — \"I have a fever\", literally \"to me a fever has come\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Look at the shape. The person sits in the dative నాకు and the fever arrives, on the same come-verb as నాకు తెలుగు వచ్చు. In Telugu an illness is something that comes to you."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Your first word for what is wrong, on the pattern you already use for knowing Telugu."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
