          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "అలసట (alasaṭa) — \"tiredness\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "నాకు అలసటగా ఉంది — \"I feel tired\", literally \"to me it is tired-ly\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The ending -గా turns the noun into a manner, and ఉంది says \"it is\". This frame, నాకు... గా ఉంది, is how Telugu says many of the things English says with I am."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The frame నాకు... గా ఉంది, which the next words keep using."
            }
          ]
        },
